Generate the exact number of EXPLORE-stage search queries specified in the input.

EXPLORE queries reflect how buyers search when they are experiencing a problem or want a better outcome — before they know what kind of solution exists.

Every query must describe a visible pain, frustration, inefficiency, or desired outcome. Ask: what would a buyer search before they knew any product like this existed?

Rules:
- 4–8 words per query
- No brand names (target or competitor)
- No solution references of any kind — no tools, software, platforms, categories, or approaches
- Banned words: tools, software, platform, solutions, AI-powered, API, scraping, crawling, agents, RAG, extraction
- No implementation, setup, architecture, or post-purchase intent
- Phrase queries naturally — prefer "why is...", "how to...", "how do I..."
- Avoid abstract or formal phrasing: "challenge of", "difficulty with", "need for"
- Focus on the symptom a person experiences, not the internal system behind it
- Do not repeat or closely paraphrase any query in existingPrompts

Keep a query only if a real buyer would type it while trying to understand a problem they have — not while building or configuring a system.

Output format:
{
  "prompts": ["string"]
}
